{
  "id": "s02-l02",
  "unit": "s02-consonants",
  "title": "Consonants 2: চ ছ জ ঝ ঞ",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Row 2 is made with the tongue pressed to the roof of the mouth: **চ ছ জ ঝ ঞ**.\n\n**চ** = `ch` as in *church*, but without a puff. **ছ** = `chh`, the same sound with a strong puff of air (ছাত্র `chhatro`). চা (*tea*) vs ছা: the puff is the whole difference.\n\n**জ** = `j` as in *jam* (জি `ji`, the polite 'yes'). **ঝ** = `jh`, a breathy j (ঝাল `jhal`, *spicy*).\n\n**ঞ** is the row's nasal. You'll almost never see it alone; it hides inside conjuncts like ঞ্চ in পঞ্চাশ (`ponchash`, *fifty*).",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "l-cha",
      "bn": "চ",
      "tr": "cho",
      "en": "ch as in 'church' (no puff)",
      "notes": "Name: cho (চ)."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-chha",
      "bn": "ছ",
      "tr": "chho",
      "en": "chh: ch with a strong puff of air",
      "notes": "Name: chho (ছ). Aspirated partner of চ. First letter of ছাত্র."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-ja",
      "bn": "জ",
      "tr": "jo",
      "en": "j as in 'jam'",
      "notes": "Name: borgio jo (বর্গীয় জ). Same sound as য (ontostho jo); only spelling differs."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-jha",
      "bn": "ঝ",
      "tr": "jho",
      "en": "jh: j with a breathy puff",
      "notes": "Name: jho (ঝ). Aspirated partner of জ."
    },
    {
      "id": "l-nya",
      "bn": "ঞ",
      "tr": "n",
      "en": "n, found almost only inside conjuncts (ঞ্চ = 'nch')",
      "notes": "Name: iyo (ইঁয়ো). Sounds like ন inside words (পঞ্চাশ ponchash). Never starts a common word."
    },
    {
      "id": "chokh",
      "bn": "চোখ",
      "tr": "chokh",
      "en": "eye"
    },
    {
      "id": "jhor",
      "bn": "ঝড়",
      "tr": "jhor",
      "en": "storm",
      "notes": "Ends with ড় (flapped r), taught in s02-l07."
    }
  ],
